WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:06.860
My grandmother [Pinky Catlon Mayo] and her sisters, they all lived . . . Aunt Minerva was her sister.

2
00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:09.920
She lived to be a hundred and eight years old.

3
00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:14.040
Then her other sister, Aunt [Lanine?] she was eighty one years old when she died.

4
00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:16.140
So . . . But they had some longevities.

5
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:20.080
Then her brother, Grandma Pinky’s brother, was Francois.

6
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.480
They called him Francis.

7
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:28.100
But he used to hop trains all the time and that’s how he got killed in the 1900s, hopping the train.

8
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:32.500
What do you think contributed to their longevity?

9
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.100
Why did they live so long?

10
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.760
Well because, you know, them back there, people lived on lands and stuff like that.

11
00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:39.160
We didn’t have all the chemicals and all that stuff.

12
00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:41.040
The lands was really rich back then.

13
00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.900
And that’s what me and my brother was talking about.

14
00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.620
We didn’t have all that sickness, the colds and all that stuff.

15
00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.000
We didn’t have all of that.

16
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.640
When we was coming up we didn’t have all of that because we lived on the land.

17
00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:50.840
We did.

18
00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.720
Everything we raised, we raised.

19
00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:58.260
Chickens, horses, we had cows, we had pigs, and that’s how people lived back then.

20
00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:04.180
And really when people died, they died mostly with pneumonia, the elder people, or they just . . . old age.
